{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:24.828915+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"NONE","body":"Update: I observed this in automatic SPMD (multi rank) calculations on sharded jax.Array's... but still trying to pin down the source of the data corruption (can't seem to be able to reproduce on single GPU)","created_at":"2024-02-03T01:22:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1924996846","id":1924996846,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yvR7u","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1924996846/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T01:56:39Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1924996846","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Just to try and make what's going on here a bit clearer to me.\r\n\r\nFirst of all, doing `X.at[idx].set(...)`, where `idx` has repeated indices, is indeed undefined behaviour in JAX (regardless of what is being set). This is what the existing warning is about / is known / is considered fine.\r\n\r\nAre you saying that you've found a case in which `idx` does *not* have repeated indices, but for which specifically the pattern `X.at[idx].set(X)` produces the wrong result? If so, that's a bug.","created_at":"2024-02-03T16:56:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1925394470","id":1925394470,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5ywzAm","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925394470/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T16:57:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925394470","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33688385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-kidger","id":33688385,"login":"patrick-kidger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg4Mzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"> Just to try and make what's going on here a bit clearer to me.\r\n> \r\n> First of all, doing `X.at[idx].set(...)`, where `idx` has repeated indices, is indeed undefined behaviour in JAX (regardless of what is being set). This is what the existing warning is about / is known / is considered fine.\r\n> \r\n> Are you saying that you've found a case in which `idx` does _not_ have repeated indices, but for which specifically the pattern `X.at[idx].set(X)` produces the wrong result? If so, that's a bug.\r\n\r\nNo, no ... I was just under the assumption that jax would do out of place transforms all the time and was surprised that it does in-place, but only under certain conditions ... (namely, jit)... so the sometimes in-place, sometimes out of place behavior seems confusing","created_at":"2024-02-03T19:50:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1925440144","id":1925440144,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yw-KQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925440144/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T19:50:32Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925440144","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Right. So logically, `.at[].set()` always operates out-of-place. But physically, the XLA compiler (the backend to JAX) will attempt to do `.at[].set()` in-place where possible.\r\n\r\nDoing this is important for performance, to avoid lots of copies of the underlying data. You'll see similar behaviour in the compilers for almost all functional languages.\r\n\r\nWhether something happens in-place or out-of-place shouldn't be observable from a user perspective, though. (Other than indirectly, through things like computation time or memory usage.) How is it that you think you're observing this distinction?","created_at":"2024-02-03T20:37:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1925449537","id":1925449537,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yxAdB","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":1,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925449537/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T20:37:30Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925449537","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33688385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-kidger","id":33688385,"login":"patrick-kidger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg4Mzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"@jglaser Here's a code sample to elaborate on what Patrick is saying:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\ndef f(x):\r\n    return x.at[3].set(0)\r\n\r\nx = jnp.arange(5)\r\nprint('x:', x)\r\n\r\nprint('\\nf(x):', f(x))\r\nprint('x after f:', x)\r\n\r\nprint('\\njit(f)(x):', jax.jit(f)(x))\r\nprint('x after jit(f):', x)\r\n\r\nprint('\\njit(f)(x) with donate:', jax.jit(f, donate_argnums=(0,))(x))\r\nprint('x after jit(f) with donate:', x)\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n# x: [0 1 2 3 4]\r\n\r\n# f(x): [0 1 2 0 4]\r\n# x after f: [0 1 2 3 4]\r\n\r\n# jit(f)(x): [0 1 2 0 4]\r\n# x after jit(f): [0 1 2 3 4]\r\n\r\n# jit(f)(x) with donate: [0 1 2 0 4]\r\n# RuntimeError: Array has been deleted with shape=int32[5].\r\n```\r\n\r\nBasically it's just that JAX will avoid doing in-place operations on transformed function _arguments_ unless explicitly given permission to. (This includes constants which your function closes over). The in-place behavior will ideally happen for intermediate tensors which you don't have direct visibility into anyways, and you can opt-in to your input arguments getting clobbered with `donate_argnums`.\r\n","created_at":"2024-02-05T01:26:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1926056571","id":1926056571,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yzUp7","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1926056571/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-05T01:26:22Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1926056571","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1377776?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davisyoshida","id":1377776,"login":"davisyoshida","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzc3NzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Hi @jglaser thanks for the report – I recall in the past XLA fixed a similar bug, where something like `x.at[idx].set(x)` would return the wrong result under JIT, but I can't seem to find the previous issue. I tried briefly to reproduce this, but wasn't able to on a CPU or GPU runtime. Would you be able to put together a minimal example of inputs for which you're seeing this problematic behavior?","created_at":"2024-02-05T13:31:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1927019837","id":1927019837,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5y2_09","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1927019837/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-05T13:31:21Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1927019837","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\r\n\r\nThe in-place modification of arrays in jax is dangerous, and behavior of \\.at[] under @jit breaks the out-of-place (functional) paradigm.\r\n\r\nThe [documentation](https://jax.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_autosummary/jax.numpy.ndarray.at.html) page carries a warning:\r\n```\r\nUnlike NumPy in-place operations such as x[idx] += y, if multiple indices refer to the same location, all updates will be applied (NumPy would only apply the last update, rather than applying all updates.) The order in which conflicting updates are applied is implementation-defined and may be nondeterministic (e.g., due to concurrency on some hardware platforms).\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, the different behavior under jit and non-jit may cause difficult to debug data issues.... Case in point\r\n\r\n```\r\n@jit\r\ndef inverse_permutation(X, idx):\r\n    return X.at[idx, :].set(X)\r\n```\r\n\r\ngiven a non-trivial permutation `idx`, this simple function will return a corrupted version of X (in my case there were nan's, luckily)...\r\n\r\nI wonder what other non-deterministic behavior usage of .at[].set() might be enabling in jax.\r\n\r\nI understand that there is a desire for performance optimization, however correctness should take precedence. Perhaps a warning could be printed if assigning an array to itself with permutation indexing.\r\n\r\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\r\n\r\n0.4.24.dev20240122+b512b576a (jax), 0.4.24.dev20240122 (jaxlib)\r\n\r\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\r\n\r\nGPU, ROCm\r\n\r\n### Additional system info?\r\n\r\nLinux login2 5.14.21-150400.24.46_12.0.83-cray_shasta_c #1 SMP Tue May 23 03:16:47 UTC 2023 (c6cda89) x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux\r\n\r\n### AMD GPU info\r\n\r\n```\r\n========================= ROCm System Management Interface =========================\r\n=================================== Concise Info ===================================\r\nGPU[1]\t\t: get_power_avg, Not supported on the given system\r\nGPU  Temp (DieEdge)  AvgPwr  SCLK    MCLK     Fan  Perf  PwrCap  VRAM%  GPU%  \r\n0    32.0c           91.0W   800Mhz  1600Mhz  0%   auto  560.0W    0%   0%    \r\n1    39.0c           N/A     800Mhz  1600Mhz  0%   auto  0.0W      0%   0%    \r\n====================================================================================\r\n=============================== End of ROCm SMI Log ================================\r\n```","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":6,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643/comments","created_at":"2024-02-03T00:53:21Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","id":2116081843,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1104782284,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTA0NzgyMjg0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOCTkjjc5-INiz","number":19643,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":2,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":2,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643/timeline","title":".at[].set() is dangerous","type":null,"updated_at":"2024-02-05T13:31:23Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","re