e_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yvR7u","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1924996846/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T01:56:39Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1924996846","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33688385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-kidger","id":33688385,"login":"patrick-kidger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg4Mzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Just to try and make what's going on here a bit clearer to me.\r\n\r\nFirst of all, doing `X.at[idx].set(...)`, where `idx` has repeated indices, is indeed undefined behaviour in JAX (regardless of what is being set). This is what the existing warning is about / is known / is considered fine.\r\n\r\nAre you saying that you've found a case in which `idx` does *not* have repeated indices, but for which specifically the pattern `X.at[idx].set(X)` produces the wrong result? If so, that's a bug.","created_at":"2024-02-03T16:56:49Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1925394470","id":1925394470,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5ywzAm","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925394470/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T16:57:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925394470","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33688385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-kidger","id":33688385,"login":"patrick-kidger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg4Mzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"NONE","body":"> Just to try and make what's going on here a bit clearer to me.\r\n> \r\n> First of all, doing `X.at[idx].set(...)`, where `idx` has repeated indices, is indeed undefined behaviour in JAX (regardless of what is being set). This is what the existing warning is about / is known / is considered fine.\r\n> \r\n> Are you saying that you've found a case in which `idx` does _not_ have repeated indices, but for which specifically the pattern `X.at[idx].set(X)` produces the wrong result? If so, that's a bug.\r\n\r\nNo, no ... I was just under the assumption that jax would do out of place transforms all the time and was surprised that it does in-place, but only under certain conditions ... (namely, jit)... so the sometimes in-place, sometimes out of place behavior seems confusing","created_at":"2024-02-03T19:50:06Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1925440144","id":1925440144,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yw-KQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925440144/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T19:50:32Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925440144","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33688385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-kidger","id":33688385,"login":"patrick-kidger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg4Mzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Right. So logically, `.at[].set()` always operates out-of-place. But physically, the XLA compiler (the backend to JAX) will attempt to do `.at[].set()` in-place where possible.\r\n\r\nDoing this is important for performance, to avoid lots of copies of the underlying data. You'll see similar behaviour in the compilers for almost all functional languages.\r\n\r\nWhether something happens in-place or out-of-place shouldn't be observable from a user perspective, though. (Other than indirectly, through things like computation time or memory usage.) How is it that you think you're observing this distinction?","created_at":"2024-02-03T20:37:30Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1925449537","id":1925449537,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yxAdB","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":1,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925449537/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-03T20:37:30Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1925449537","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33688385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/patrick-kidger","id":33688385,"login":"patrick-kidger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNjg4Mzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrick-kidger","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1377776?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davisyoshida","id":1377776,"login":"davisyoshida","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzc3NzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"@jglaser Here's a code sample to elaborate on what Patrick is saying:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\ndef f(x):\r\n    return x.at[3].set(0)\r\n\r\nx = jnp.arange(5)\r\nprint('x:', x)\r\n\r\nprint('\\nf(x):', f(x))\r\nprint('x after f:', x)\r\n\r\nprint('\\njit(f)(x):', jax.jit(f)(x))\r\nprint('x after jit(f):', x)\r\n\r\nprint('\\njit(f)(x) with donate:', jax.jit(f, donate_argnums=(0,))(x))\r\nprint('x after jit(f) with donate:', x)\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n# x: [0 1 2 3 4]\r\n\r\n# f(x): [0 1 2 0 4]\r\n# x after f: [0 1 2 3 4]\r\n\r\n# jit(f)(x): [0 1 2 0 4]\r\n# x after jit(f): [0 1 2 3 4]\r\n\r\n# jit(f)(x) with donate: [0 1 2 0 4]\r\n# RuntimeError: Array has been deleted with shape=int32[5].\r\n```\r\n\r\nBasically it's just that JAX will avoid doing in-place operations on transformed function _arguments_ unless explicitly given permission to. (This includes constants which your function closes over). The in-place behavior will ideally happen for intermediate tensors which you don't have direct visibility into anyways, and you can opt-in to your input arguments getting clobbered with `donate_argnums`.\r\n","created_at":"2024-02-05T01:26:22Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643#issuecomment-1926056571","id":1926056571,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19643","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5yzUp7","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1926056571/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-05T01:26:22Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1926056571","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1377776?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davisyoshida","id":1377776,"login":"davisyoshida","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzc3NzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davisyoshida","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1899768?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jglaser","id":1899768,"login":"jglaser","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTk3Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jglaser","user_view_type":"public"},"commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2024-02-05T01:26:24Z","event":"mentioned","id":11697471310,"node_id":"MEE_lADOCTkjjc5-INizzwAAAAK5OT9O","performed_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://a